Data: the piano boot DT (out/inputs/piano-boot.dtb, sha256 50636effb5f54306ec0ab9a3061cd163d7f003d8797e04585a33205918856840): the
Iris node (address, interrupt, streams, firmware-name, memory-region), the videocc node, the video@9c300000 carveout, the apps
SMMU's dma-coherent property, the video thermal zone; for levels 2-4 the node's resets and interconnects, the rpmhpd OPP levels
(the 240 MHz OPP's required MXC svs / MMCX low_svs_d1, VIDEO_CC's low_svs), the mdss/DPU OPP table (575 MHz requires MMCX
NOM_L1: the display floor), the cmd-db and DRV-2 reservations. xiaomipad-8pro-mainline firmware/piano-iris.json: the firmware's
name, size and pin (the file itself is the owner's, read at run time, never in this repository; when it is on the build Mac,
tests/bringup_host.cpp hashes it and parses its ELF and program headers, as the secure world's loader takes them).

Not read and not used for anything: any Qualcomm or Xiaomi binary beyond that (vpu35_4v.mbn is data for the secure world's
loader, never disassembled), Apple binaries beyond public headers and class/symbol names.
